The purpose of modeling SRLGs (Shared Risk Link Groups) in inventory is to identify and manage groups of network resources that share a common risk factor, which could lead to service outages. By modeling SRLGs, network operators can ensure redundancy and resilience in their network design, effectively mitigating the impact of failures that may affect multiple links simultaneously.

SRLGs are typically represented in a structured format that includes identifiers for the links in the group, their risk attributes, and any associated metadata. This can be depicted as JSON structured data:

```json
{
  "SRLGs": [
    {
      "id": "SRLG-001",
      "links": [
        "Link-1",
        "Link-2",
        "Link-3"
      ],
      "risk_factor": "fiber_cable_damage",
      "description": "This group shares the same fiber path, hence risk of failure."
    },
    {
      "id": "SRLG-002",
      "links": [
        "Link-4",
        "Link-5"
      ],
      "risk_factor": "electrical_interference",
      "description": "These links traverse an area prone to electromagnetic interference."
    }
  ]
}
```

