The NMS/script can determine which value corresponds to which requested OID by examining the structure of the SNMP GET Response PDU. The PDU includes a sequence of variable bindings, where each binding consists of an OID and its corresponding value. The alignments of these OIDs with the values in the response allow the NMS/script to directly match the values to the requested OIDs.

In structured form, the response can be conceptualized as follows:

```json
{
  "response": {
    "version": "SNMPv2c",
    "type": "GET_RESPONSE",
    "request_id": "12345",
    "variable_bindings": [
      {
        "oid": "1.3.6.1.2.1.1.1.0",
        "value": "Linux server 5.4.0"
      },
      {
        "oid": "1.3.6.1.2.1.1.2.0",
        "value": "123456"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

This structure indicates that the values "Linux server 5.4.0" and "123456" correspond to the OIDs "1.3.6.1.2.1.1.1.0" and "1.3.6.1.2.1.1.2.0", respectively.

