To implement port mirroring (SPAN) using a firewall filter, you can configure the firewall to mirror the traffic of a specific port or VLAN to a designated monitoring port. This is done by defining a firewall filter action that specifies the source and destination of the mirrored traffic. Below is an example configuration in JSON format:

```json
{
  "firewall-filter": {
    "name": "port-mirror-filter",
    "actions": {
      "port-mirror": {
        "source-port": "eth0",
        "destination-port": "monitor-port"
      }
    },
    "rules": [
      {
        "action": "port-mirror",
        "match": {
          "traffic-type": "all"
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
``` 

In this configuration, all traffic from `eth0` will be mirrored to `monitor-port`.

