To load configuration changes provided in standard Junos brace {} hierarchy format using PyEZ, you can use the `load()` method from a device object with the `format='text'` argument as follows:

```python
from jnpr.junos import Device

# Establish a connection to the device
dev = Device(host='host_name', user='user_name', password='password')
dev.open()

# Load configuration in brace format
config = """
{
    system {
        host-name junos-device;
        time-zone UTC;
    }
    interfaces {
        ge-0/0/0 {
            description "Uplink";
            unit 0 {
                family inet {
                    address 192.0.2.1/24;
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
"""

# Load the configuration
dev.load(config, format='text')

# Commit the changes
dev.commit()

# Close the connection
dev.close()
```

