To perform Tricolor Marking using a firewall filter with a policer, you can configure the policer to evaluate packets based on their traffic characteristics: Committed Information Rate (CIR), Committed Burst Size (CBS), Peak Information Rate (PIR), and Peak Burst Size (PBS). The configuration dictates how packets are marked as Green (within limits), Yellow (exceeding limits but within threshold), or Red (exceeding maximum allowance).

